# The 1983 source: FIELD's total past the record is FIELD overflow (DSKCOM.ASM's TEMPB against TEMPA; PC-BASIC lets 15 + 6 into 20); a record past 32767 is taken (the IBM manual's p. 113 and A-4; the IBM spec's fix-up, C-1 item 12: the source's JLE refused it), and -1 is Bad record number; the FIELD buffer isn't cleared by anything but the bytes written (line 150's tail now shows the zeros GET #1,32768 read from a record never written, as PC-BASIC's does); INPUT # and PRINT # share FD_OPS, and WRITE # pads the record with spaces to two bytes from its end, then CR LF (FIVEO.ASM's WRTFIN, CMPFBC; PC-BASIC doesn't pad)
